= 2.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"strained\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"C\",\n      \"strongest_reading\": \"Reversing the difference gives 28 − 30 = −2, but the fifth unit’s change is measured from four units to five.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"strained\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"D\",\n      \"strongest_reading\": \"One might report total utility after five units, but the stem asks for marginal utility, the one-unit change, which is 2.\",\n      \"correct_under_reading\": false,\n      \"reading_status\": \"contradicts_stem\",\n      \"convention_evidence_ids\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocking_defects\": [],\n  \"style_notes\": [],\n  \"cuet_fit\": {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"syllabus_objective\": {\n        \"level\": 2,\n        \"evidence\": \"Utility calculations support the syllabus’s utility-approach objective; MU itself is a standard supporting concept.\"\n      },\n      \"format_authenticity\": {\n        \"level\": 3,\n        \"evidence\": \"A concise four-option numerical MCQ, consistent with the authenticated economics examples.\"\n      },\n      \"level_calibration\": {\n        \"level\": 2,\n        \"evidence\": \"A simple one-step subtraction is within the numerical range, but easier than the supplied calculation comparators.\"\n      },\n      \"discrimination_value\": {\n        \"level\": 3,\n        \"evidence\": \"The distractors reflect identifiable confusions: unit count, reversed change, and total versus marginal utility.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"reasoning_steps\": 1,\n    \"estimated_difficulty\": \"easy\",\n    \"cognitive_level\": \"application\",\n    \"exemplar_ids_compared\": [\n      \"cuet2024-economics-bookA-q2\",\n      \"cuet2024-economics-bookA-q46\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"option_resolution\": [\n    {\n      \"option\": \"A\",\n      \"status\": \"supported\",\n      \"false_part\": \"\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"excerpt\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"E1.1\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"consumption of the 5th banana has caused total utility to increase by 2 units (30 units minus 28 units).\",\n      \"reason\": \"The same total-utility values yield a fifth-unit marginal utility of 30 − 28 = 2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"B\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"5\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"Total utility is 28 after four units and 30 after five.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The change is 30 − 28 = 2, not 5.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"C\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"−2\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"Total utility is 28 after four units and 30 after five.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The change from four to five units is 30 − 28 = 2, not −2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"option\": \"D\",\n      \"status\": \"contradicted\",\n      \"false_part\": \"30\",\n      \"premise_source\": \"arithmetic\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"\",\n      \"premise_quote\": \"Total utility is 28 after four units and 30 after five.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Marginal utility is the change, 30 − 28 = 2; 30 is the five-unit total utility.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
